I forgot about him.

264
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:05,857
I'm sure he's around here somewhere.

265
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,293
But where is somewhere?

266
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:09,137
I haven't seen him for a while.

267
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,573
Not since we descended.

268
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:13,837
Do you think he might have been
thrown off when everything went crazy?

269
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:14,920
Totally possible.

270
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,997
I mean, his arms and legs were tied up.

271
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:19,997
There's no way he could hold on to
anything while we were rocking around.

272
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,256
Normally, I'd agree.

273
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:24,860
But it seems that he freed himself. Look.

274
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:31,057
so that Drop weirdo escaped and he's still

275
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:34,557
here he's got to be
waiting us out for a moment

276
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:40,617
to attack this is bad
if you're so eager to

277
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:42,957
see me i'd be happy to
sneak into your room

278
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,937
tonight sweetheart damn
it we've got enough

279
00:15:46,020 --> 00:15:47,857
problems we don't need
this guy giving us one

280
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:50,577
more thing to worry
about don't get worked up

281
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:53,484
it's not like he's an
actual threat to any of us

282
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,757
That's right, you think that.

283
00:15:56,840 --> 00:16:00,037
You'll see how wrong you are now
that the three morons who could

284
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:04,180
put up a fight have gotten themselves
killed fighting that kraken.

285
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:06,800
After all,

286
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:09,957
there's no way they survive
getting sucked down into the bowels

287
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:13,452
of the ocean with just those
tiny bubbles to protect them.

288
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:18,357
What a shame I didn't have the chance
to kill Straw Hat with my own hands.

289
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:22,077
But no one will ever doubt that
he's dead once I come back with

290
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:25,837
the rest of his crew members heads
in tow as my personal trophies.

291
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,440
No one at all.

292
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,857
But I can't get too excited.

293
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:33,577
There's no need to rush.

294
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:37,497
If I killed them all now, there wouldn't
be anyone left to sail the ship!

295
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:39,051
And then what would I do?

296
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:42,777
So I'll let them live for now while
they can still be useful to me.

297
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:48,260
Once we land on Fishman Island though, I'm
gonna slaughter you down to the last man!

298
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,957
Let's see a break out of that.

299
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,257
How did he even manage to
get in there because we

300
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:23,097
weren't paying attention to
him if he weren't so stupid?

301
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:24,477
We could have been in trouble.

302
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:27,207
His body was like a big
mass of goo in there.

303
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:30,017
It didn't have a real shape
So he was like a pile of mud.

304
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:32,747
Yeah, if I had to guess
the Devil Fruit power

305
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,117
Most likely a logia type fruit at
that he was giving us a false sense

306
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:41,217
of security because he could have
escaped at any time Get me out of here!

307
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,535
I'll behave, I swear!

308
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:46,637
You and the banana hammock, and if
you let me out, I'll be your servant!

309
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,550
Come on!

310
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:54,484
You feeling all right, Chopper?

311
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:55,760
I don't know.

312
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:57,760
It just got really hot.

313
00:17:58,280 --> 00:17:59,940
I can't stand the heat.

314
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:01,240
I'm dying.

315
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,030
Chouchou!

316
00:18:03,113 --> 00:18:04,020
It is warmer.

317
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,080
Wait a second. Is that smoke?

318
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:10,144
We can't see what's in
front of us through that!

319
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,774
Smoke under the water?

320
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,190
Can't be.

321
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:15,380
Actually, it can.

322
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,360
Is that...

323
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:25,293
Hydro-thermal deposits.

324
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:26,290
What?

325
00:18:26,373 --> 00:18:27,203
Keep up.

326
00:18:27,286 --> 00:18:29,520
This is a volcanic area. For real?

327
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:30,840
Yes, for real.

328
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:33,237
You can see where there
have been eruptions.

329
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,144
We have to get out of here now.

330
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:38,025
If one of those erupts,
we're just gonna stand.

331
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,117
It's hot.

332
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,500
I'm so hot.

333
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,697
There's something coming after us!

334
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:47,500
It's carnivorous tube worms!

335
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,740
You've got no choice. Small one.

336
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,260
Coup de burst!

337
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,460
Chase those crabs!

338
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:59,880
Have to risk it again. Coup de burst!

339
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:03,457
I don't even know what
the hell those things are!

340
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:04,370
Hang on, guys.

341
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,700
Coup de burst!

342
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,437
The sea is awful.

343
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,440
I hate it.

344
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:12,437
There's no way the others can
survive down here on their own.

345
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,977
I can't believe this is happening!

346
00:19:15,060 --> 00:19:17,177
And we'd only just gotten back together.

347
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:18,090
Stop crying.

348
00:19:18,173 --> 00:19:20,297
Those three are way too tough to die.

349
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:25,580
Even using coup to burst that sparingly,
we've lost so much air already.

350
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:30,457
What is that?

351
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:32,157
A light in the darkness.

352
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,197
Wait.

353
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,877
Is that Fishman Island?

354
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:37,217
Maybe Luffy beat us there.

355
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:38,520
It can't be.

356
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,957
We haven't descended
the last 3,000 meters.

357
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:41,880
Who are you?

358
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,000
A friend?

359
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:44,390
Stop!

360
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:47,417
If you want to flash signals,
do it without actually flashing!

361
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:48,817
Can you tell what it is?

362
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,841
No, it's still too bright to see.

363
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:54,910
Oh, no!

364
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:00,600
An anglerfish! We're screwed!

365
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:03,245
The deep-sea hunter fooled us.

366
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:04,811
Hook, line, and sink her!

367
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:09,620
A little close that time!

368
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:11,897
There isn't anywhere left for us to run.

369
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:13,120
What can we do?

370
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,520
This can't be happening!

371
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:23,180
It's human?

372
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:25,107
No, this isn't making a sea!

373
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:26,580
A sea monster?

374
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:29,320
That's taking the form of a man!

375
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,600
It's a sea monster!

376
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:39,520
He's going to capsize the ship!

377
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:44,900
What the?

378
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,660
Hey, that's naughty.

379
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:48,520
You know better, Ancaro.

380
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,462
You're not allowed to eat ships.

381
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:54,280
How many times do I have to tell you?

382
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:59,327
Captain Vandor Deccan won't be
happy when he hears about this.

383
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,400
Wait, did he just help us?

384
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:03,420
Who freaking cares?

385
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,077
Let's just make a break for it.

386
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,631
He might change his mind.

387
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,720
Dead men tell no tales,
and dead men have mercy.

388
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:22,780
I pluck the rings right off their
hands within these shadowy seas.

389
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:28,180
Dead men have no regrets
and no tears left to weep.

390
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:33,757
I'll pluck the crowns right off their
heads within this cold, black deep.

391
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:38,017
Sunken treasures free
for the taking A king

392
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:41,677
of pirates in the making
I leave my enemies

393
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:45,957
weeping and shaking Vander Decken is my

394
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:51,240
name And these long-lost riches I do claim

395
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:56,340
No way!

396
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,120
Now we can't be!

397
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:10,100
It's a ghost ship!

398
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:12,751
You are the last one who should be scared!

399
00:22:12,980 --> 00:22:16,568
Nothing would make me happier,
but take a look at their sail!

400
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:20,560
That's the legendary Flying Dutchman!

401
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:22,240
It shouldn't be here!

402
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:23,558
It shouldn't exist!

403
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:27,960
As the story goes, it sailed
the seas hundreds of years ago.

404
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:33,440
One dark and stormy night, the captain
of the ship suddenly lost his mind.

405
00:22:33,900 --> 00:22:38,665
Consumed with madness, he threw his own
crewmates into the sea one after another.

406
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:42,645
Then he turned his gaze to the
heavens and cursed the very gods.

407
00:22:42,940 --> 00:22:45,957
The captain's name was none
other than Vander Decken,

408
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:48,660
and the ship was the Flying Dutchman.

409
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:54,060
The gods condemned him for his actions,
and he was cursed for all eternity.

410
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,277
Sailing the seas aimlessly.

411
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:58,077
Theron and Mary Vassal.

412
00:22:58,160 --> 00:23:00,437
Even if you're a skeleton who has sailed.

413
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:01,677
On a ghost ship of your own.

414
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,317
The sight of the flying Dutchman.

415
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:05,217
Will put chills down your spine.

416
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,317
Listen up.

417
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:09,237
I'm not digging their
treasure out of your stomachs.

418
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,537
So no eating the ship.

419
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:12,660
Just give it a good knock.

420
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:15,377
You bitch.

421
00:23:15,460 --> 00:23:18,637
I think we're about to get pounded.

422
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:20,477
Well sure, he's our enemy.

423
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,637
Franky, we need a coup de purse.

424
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:24,000
I can't.

425
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:26,022
We used up all our fuel already.

426
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:30,046
That means we're on our own till
I can restock the cola supply.

427
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:46,587
That's the monster of
the Arctic, the Kraken.

428
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,760
You big boy!

429
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:56,700
All right, he learned his lesson. Enough!

430
00:24:00,560 --> 00:24:01,800
Good boy.

431
00:24:06,340 --> 00:24:07,170
Hey!

432
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:11,800
Guys, I thought you were dead!

433
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:14,260
That was so scary!

434
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:16,905
What the heck happened to you?

435
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:19,200
Mommy Swan! Robin!

436
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,800
It was crazy, that's for sure!

437
00:24:24,820 --> 00:24:26,600
They got lost. Morons.

438
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,527
They're hopeless without me.

439
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:30,640
Are you gonna take that, Watasumi?

440
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:31,860
Get back up!

441
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:34,260
Avenge yourself! Start swinging!

442
00:24:37,140 --> 00:24:39,520
My bubble popped and so did Sanji,

443
00:24:39,660 --> 00:24:42,895
so we all had to crowd inside
Zoro's before he drowned!

444
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,700
We're running out of air!

445
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:47,397
How about you stop scaring us like that?

446
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:50,057
Now a song for you, captain?

447
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:57,140
No

448
00:24:57,460 --> 00:25:02,117
kidding,

449
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:04,657
and you tamed the kraken
just like you said.

450
00:25:04,740 --> 00:25:06,257
I thought you were nuts.

451
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:09,540
So is he going to be our new guy?

452
00:25:10,180 --> 00:25:11,010
Yeah!

453
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:13,557
If that Cape dude can have
a sea monster pull his ship,

454
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:15,417
then we can have Tsurume pull the Sunny!

455
00:25:15,500 --> 00:25:16,330
Right, pal?

456
00:25:16,413 --> 00:25:19,221
Of course you would name
it already, wouldn't you?

457
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:22,137
That's cool if he wants
to give us a free ride.

458
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:25,808
But make sure he doesn't crush
us with those giant tentacles.

459
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:31,810
What's that?

460
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:37,700
Captain, stop!

461
00:25:38,060 --> 00:25:40,001
We gotta turn back or we're dead!

462
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:42,300
I knew it.

463
00:25:42,460 --> 00:25:43,636
An undersea volcano.

464
00:25:44,040 --> 00:25:44,980
Straight ahead!
